<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav Jan industry output falls 20.8 pct vs Dec.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav Jan industry output falls 20.8 pct vs Dec.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistical Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT  JAN 97	DEC 96	JAN 96</p>
<p> pct change mth/mth	   - 20.8	-  2.0	 - 13.4</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr	     +  2.9	+  4.8	  + 9.7</p>
<p> index (base average 1996)    87.8	 116.2	   96.1</p>
<p>SEASONALLY ADJUSTED DATA</p>
<p> index (base average 1996)   101.7	 100.0	  102.9</p>
<p>NOTES - Industrial output in 1996 was 7.5 percent higher than in 1995.</p>
<p>Industrial output in January 1997 was 51.9 percent lower than in January 1991, before the breakup of former Yugoslavia.</p>
<p>Industrial output in January 1997 was 12.2 percent below the average monthly production in 1996.</p>
<p>Data largely exclude the private sector, where manufacturing is not significant.</p>
<p>-- Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 222 4305</p>
</text>
